# Council of Echoes: the "if there are four or more permanent cards in your graveyard" (CR 603.4, 110.4a) counts Bot1's graveyard only.
# Bot1 has three there when Council enters: two Plains milled by Thought Scour and Black Lotus, sacrificed for mana as Council is cast
# (Thought Scour and Hymn to Tourach are not permanent cards). Hymn to Tourach also put two Ornithopters into Bot2's graveyard, five
# permanent cards in all, which do not count: the trigger never goes on the stack (with a target to choose among Bot2's Ornithopter and
# Bot1's Moxen it would have stopped for one), so nothing returns. (The scenarios with exactly four are the positive controls.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Mox Jet
Thought Scour
Hymn to Tourach
Black Lotus
Council of Echoes
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thought Scour.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hymn to Tourach.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Council of Echoes.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 5
! Bot1.Target()
? Stack.Count = 0

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 2
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield = Council of Echoes; Mox Jet; Mox Jet; Mox Sapphire
